# 28. Common INSERT Mistakes

## Mistake 1 — Wrong number of values

Table:

```text
student_id
student_name
age
```

Wrong:

```sql
INSERT INTO students
VALUES (101, 'Ravi');
```

There are only two values for three columns.

---

## Mistake 2 — Wrong order

Suppose:

```text
student_id
student_name
age
```

Then:

```sql
VALUES ('Ravi', 101, 20);
```

is the wrong order.

Prefer specifying columns:

```sql
INSERT INTO students
    (student_id, student_name, age)
VALUES
    (101, 'Ravi', 20);
```

---

## Mistake 3 — Forgetting quotes for text

Wrong:

```sql
VALUES (101, Ravi, 20);
```

Correct:

```sql
VALUES (101, 'Ravi', 20);
```

---

# 29. Common UPDATE Mistakes

### Mistake 1 — Forgetting WHERE

Dangerous:

```sql
UPDATE students
SET age = 25;
```

This may update every row.

---

### Mistake 2 — Wrong condition

For example:

```sql
UPDATE students
SET age = 25
WHERE student_id = 999;
```

If ID `999` doesn't exist, no row may be changed.

Always verify the condition.

---

# 30. Common DELETE Mistakes

### Mistake 1 — Forgetting WHERE

```sql
DELETE FROM students;
```

This removes all rows.

If you only intended to remove one student, this is a serious mistake.

